Changelog

3.4.0  2026-05-16  Markdown as a first-class entry format (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.8)

	Storage formats — honest names + new MARKDOWN
	-The InformationFormat names finally match reality: ASCII→TEXT
	 (it has been UTF-8/UTF-16 since the Qt6 port, never ASCII) and
	 RTF→HTML (getText() returns toHtml(); there were never any RTF
	 bytes). The vestigial NONE was dropped. Old data files keep
	 loading — the XML reader accepts both the new and the legacy
	 format names; only the new names are written.
	-New MARKDOWN format. Markdown entries store the raw .md source
	 and are rendered on demand via Qt's bundled md4c. Import/export
	 of .md round-trips through the MARKDOWN format instead of
	 silently turning into HTML.

	Editor — Markdown UX
	-Markdown entries open in a read-only rendered VIEW by default
	 (viewing/searching is the common case); a "✎ Edit" toolbar
	 toggle switches to editing the source. The rendered view is a
	 separate read-only widget — selection and copy work, the editor
	 document is never mutated, so the source's full undo/redo history
	 survives toggling view↔edit.
	-Optional live split-view preview pane (Options → Markdown, off
	 by default): source and rendered output side by side.
	-Markdown insert helpers (bold/italic/code/heading/lists/link/
	 fence/table) on the toolbar, shown only while editing a MARKDOWN
	 entry.
	-Tree right-click "Change format" submenu converts an entry
	 between TEXT / HTML / MARKDOWN (full cross-conversion via
	 QTextDocument). The legacy toolbar "Convert format" button now
	 works HTML↔TEXT too.

	Plain-text correctness
	-In TEXT/MARKDOWN modes the rich-text toolbar (bold/italic/colors/
	 fonts/lists) is hidden, paste drops formatting, and content is
	 saved as plain text in the configured editor font. New "Reset
	 formatting of selection" action (Edit menu + editor right-click)
	 clears formatting on the selection only and is undoable.
	-Options font pickers (editor / tree) now show the size, not just
	 the family.

	(LaTeX math and Graphviz-diagram rendering in the preview were
	prototyped on this branch but pulled out for a separate, redesigned
	feature later — kept on branch archive/md-math-diagrams-JKQTMathText.)

3.3.3  2026-05-16  Shortcut rebalance: Ctrl+F back to tree search, F3 for in-entry find (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	The 3.3 series had moved Ctrl+F onto the in-editor find/replace
	bar (with tree search shoved to Ctrl+Shift+F + an F7 fallback for
	WMs that grab Ctrl+Shift). In practice Ctrl+F-in-editor turned
	out uncomfortable for the muscle-memory crowd, so:

	-Ctrl+F = "search across the whole tree" again (its meaning
	 pre-3.3).
	-F3 = "find in current entry". Smart open-or-next: first press
	 opens the editor find bar, subsequent presses advance to the
	 next match. Shift+F3 = previous match.
	-Ctrl+H = in-entry find+replace, unchanged.
	-Ctrl+Shift+F and the F7 fallback are removed.

	The editor find bar's internal F3 QShortcut is dropped to avoid
	"Ambiguous shortcut overload" with the new MainWindow QAction.
	Shift+F3 inside the bar stays. EditorFindBar::findNext/findPrev
	are promoted from private to public slots so MainWindow can drive
	them directly. Russian UI updated for the new strings (307/307).

3.3.2  2026-05-16  Build fix: switch translations pipeline to qt_add_translations() (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	Follow-up to 3.3.1. The earlier add_dependencies(tuxcards
	tuxcards_translations) was not sufficient because AUTORCC of the
	generated .qrc runs as its own CMake sub-target
	(tuxcards_arcc_translations_generated) and doesn't inherit the
	parent's dependencies — so rcc still raced lrelease on parallel
	builds. The hand-rolled qt_add_lrelease + file(GENERATE) .qrc is
	replaced by the high-level qt_add_translations() helper, which
	goes through qt_add_resources (not AUTORCC) and wires the
	ordering correctly. Same end result, no read-side behavior change.

3.3.1  2026-05-16  Build fix: AUTORCC ordering for generated translations .qrc (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	The 3.3.0 release tag triggered a release.yml run that succeeded on
	pre-6.7 Qt (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 12, Windows install-qt-action) but
	failed everywhere the new build-dir translations qrc actually got
	exercised (Ubuntu 26.04, Debian 13, macOS, Fedora .rpm). Root cause:
	AUTORCC scanned build/translations_generated.qrc before the
	tuxcards_translations target produced the .qm files it references.
	Fix: add an explicit add_dependencies(tuxcards tuxcards_translations).
	Behavior unchanged on the read side; only the CMake target graph.

3.3.0  2026-05-16  In-editor find/replace, lazy-decrypt, print preview, refactors (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	Editor — in-entry find & replace
	-New embedded find/replace bar at the bottom of the editor
	 (Ctrl+F = Find, Ctrl+H = Find + Replace). Case-sensitive and
	 whole-word toggles, wrap-around, status messages ("not found",
	 "(wrapped)", "N replacement(s)"), Esc to close, F3 / Shift+F3
	 for next/previous. Replace works browser-style: first click
	 selects the next match, second click substitutes — so an
	 unexpected match never gets quietly overwritten.
	-Tree-wide Search dialog moved to Ctrl+Shift+F (was Ctrl+F).
	 Standard IDE convention frees Ctrl+F for in-entry search.
	-F7 fallback wired up for the tree search action — on Linux
	 desktops where Ctrl+Shift is grabbed by the keyboard-layout
	 switcher and never reaches Qt.
	-Find / Replace / Tree search exposed as proper QAction entries
	 in the Edit menu (with Qt::WindowShortcut), replacing the old
	 keyPressEvent dispatch.

	Encryption — optional lazy decrypt
	-New Options → Encryption checkbox "Decrypt entries only when
	 viewed (faster open of large files)". When enabled, opening an
	 encrypted file only verifies the password against one entry and
	 leaves the rest as ciphertext; entries get decrypted on the
	 first navigation. Saves untouched entries by emitting the
	 on-disk ciphertext byte-for-byte (already supported by the 3.2
	 mOriginalBlob/mbDirty path).
	-The Search dialog notices entries that are still encrypted and
	 reports them as "(N encrypted entry not scanned — open it once
	 to include it)".

	File — print preview
	-New "Print pre&view..." entry in the File menu and a separate
	 toolbar button bound to Ctrl+Shift+P. Renders the current entry
	 via QPrintPreviewDialog; the direct-print action and its Ctrl+P
	 shortcut are unchanged.

	Window — persisted geometry
	-Window X/Y position is now stored in ~/.tuxcards alongside the
	 existing width/height (-1 sentinel = "let the window manager
	 pick"), so reopening the app restores the prior placement on
	 WMs that don't remember it themselves.
	-Tree vertical-scrollbar restore is deferred to a queued event
	 so the saved position survives even when the tree's row layout
	 isn't ready yet at load time.

	Build / packaging
	-CMake auto-falls back TUXCARDS_WRITE_BACKEND to monocypher when
	 the OpenSSL backend is disabled (e.g. legacy
	 -DTUXCARDS_WITH_OPENSSL=OFF), instead of failing the configure.
	-Translation pipeline now generates an in-build-dir translations
	 .qrc that points at the .qm files lrelease just produced.
	 Refreshing translations after lupdate no longer needs the manual
	 copy of build/*.qm back into translations/ + touch of the .qrc.

	Tests
	-tst_stringcrypter gains a fixture test that verifies the legacy
	 Blowfish+MD5 magic ("Fh_enc:BF10") is still detected by
	 identifyBlobFormat() on a real 2010-era encrypted blob, locking
	 in backward-compat reading of pre-2.0 tuxcards files.

	Refactors (no behavior change)
	-All 163 SIGNAL()/SLOT() macro-style connects converted to the
	 Qt5+ pointer-to-member syntax, so signal/slot signature
	 mismatches now surface as compile errors instead of runtime
	 silent disconnects. MainWindow::open()/save() overloads are
	 disambiguated with qOverload<>.
	-CInformationElement::mpChildObjects (heap-allocated
	 QList<T*>*) collapsed to mChildObjects (QList<T*> by value) —
	 one fewer heap alloc per node, removes a class of double-free
	 risk on tree teardown, getChildren() public signature unchanged.
	-Dropped the redundant Ctrl+F / Ctrl+H / Ctrl+Shift+F dispatch
	 in MainWindow::keyPressEvent — the new Edit-menu QActions fire
	 them via Qt's shortcut system.
	-Silenced -Wunused-result on the optional system() exec hook
	 (callingExecutionStatement).
	-Removed the obsolete docs/en/ tree (TuxCards 2010 HTML manual).

3.2.0  2026-05-16  Multi-backend crypto, save-freeze fix, full Russian UI (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	Crypto — save/load performance
	-Save no longer freezes the UI on encrypted files. The serializer
	 used to call encrypt() and then decrypt() for every encrypted
	 node — two PBKDF2(200 000) passes per element — and on a 30-note
	 tree that burned 6–9 seconds on the UI thread. The fix encrypts
	 to a local buffer without mutating in-memory state.
	-Process-wide session key cache in StringCrypter: AES-GCM and
	 XChaCha both derive their key once per save/load burst instead
	 of once per element. clearKeyCache() is wired in MainWindow on
	 file open / close / clearAll so the derived key doesn't outlive
	 the open file.
	-Dirty-tracking on each entry: the in-memory copy of the original
	 ciphertext (mOriginalBlob) is kept alongside the plaintext;
	 on save, untouched entries are emitted byte-for-byte without
	 a cipher call. Editing an entry flags it dirty and triggers
	 a fresh re-encrypt on the next save.

	Crypto — new XChaCha20-Poly1305 + Argon2i backend
	-Second crypto backend via vendored monocypher 4.0.2
	 (~3000 LoC, public domain / BSD-2 dual licence; single .c/.h
	 in src/utilities/crypt/monocypher/, no system dependency).
	 New on-disk blob format "Fh_enc:XChaCha20Poly1305-Argon2i-v1"
	 with memory-hard Argon2i KDF (64 MB / 3 passes / 1 lane
	 defaults, capped at 256 MB / 32 passes / 16 lanes on read).
	-CMake options: TUXCARDS_BACKEND_OPENSSL,
	 TUXCARDS_BACKEND_MONOCYPHER (both ON by default),
	 TUXCARDS_WRITE_BACKEND (openssl | monocypher, default openssl).
	 At least one backend must be ON; the write backend must match
	 an ON backend — CMake errors out otherwise.
	-The decryptString() dispatcher routes by magic header so one
	 binary reads all three formats: AES-256-GCM, XChaCha20-Poly1305,
	 and the legacy BF10 (Blowfish + MD5) format from TuxCards 2.0.
	 Backwards compatibility: the legacy TUXCARDS_WITH_OPENSSL=OFF
	 knob still works and is treated as TUXCARDS_BACKEND_OPENSSL=OFF.
	-Options → Encryption tab: pick the cipher used for new entries
	 (AES-256-GCM via OpenSSL, or XChaCha20-Poly1305 + Argon2i via
	 monocypher). Each entry remembers the format it was written in;
	 by default only edited entries get re-encrypted on save, so the
	 file can contain mixed formats. Tick "Re-encrypt all entries
	 when the algorithm changes" to force a homogeneous re-write.
	-If a file is encrypted with an algorithm not linked into this
	 build, the open flow now shows a "Unsupported encryption format"
	 dialog naming the missing backend and pointing the user to a
	 full build — instead of looping on "wrong password".

	Release matrix
	-Windows and macOS release jobs split into matrices of
	 {openssl, noopenssl} variants:
	   tuxcards-qt6-<ver>-windows-x64.zip            (AES-GCM + XChaCha)
	   tuxcards-qt6-<ver>-windows-x64-noopenssl.zip  (XChaCha only)
	   tuxcards-qt6-<ver>-macos.dmg                  (AES-GCM + XChaCha)
	   tuxcards-qt6-<ver>-macos-noopenssl.dmg        (XChaCha only)
	 The -noopenssl macOS DMG ships without a bundled libcrypto and
	 is ~3 MB smaller; it can still read XChaCha + legacy BF10 blobs.

	Tests
	-tst_stringcrypter grew XChaCha round-trip / wrong-password /
	 tampered-ciphertext / cross-backend-dispatch cases. 14/14 green
	 under both write backends.

	Localization
	-tr()-wrapping pass over the C++ GUI: ~170 user-visible literals
	 in mainwindow.cpp, optionsdialog.cpp (SideBar tab), CTree.cpp,
	 editor.cpp, searchdialog.cpp, CPropertyDialog.cpp,
	 iconselectordialog.cpp, CTuxCardsConfiguration.cpp,
	 CFileEncryptionPasswordDialog.cpp and CPasswdDialog.cpp that
	 lived as bare string literals since TuxCards 2.0 are now
	 translatable via tr(). Total translatable strings in .ts files
	 grew from 102 to 277.
	-tuxcards_ru.ts is fully translated for the new strings.
	 Translations for de / es / fr / pt_BR / ja / ko / zh_CN / zh_TW
	 remain as unfinished slots ready for community PRs.

	Dialog polish
	-IFileEncryptionPasswordDialog (the "enter password" prompt)
	 reworked: the Qt 3-era absolute-position layout was replaced
	 with a proper QVBoxLayout. The dialog now sizes to its contents,
	 centers itself on the parent window before show(), and has its
	 OK / Cancel buttons centered as a group with consistent
	 90 px-wide buttons.
	-IPasswdDialog (the "set password on toggle" prompt) gets the
	 same treatment: centered OK / Cancel via balanced spacers and
	 a centered window. The duplicate buttonOk → accept() connection
	 (set both in the .ui and in C++) was removed — it was firing
	 accept() twice on each click.

	Internal
	-StringCrypter exposes identifyBlobFormat(),
	 isBackendAvailableFor(), setWriteBackend()/getWriteBackend()
	 and a new ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_BACKEND error code. The dispatcher
	 in MainWindow::initializingCollection() peeks at the first
	 encrypted blob in the tree before prompting for a password,
	 so we don't loop on wrong-password when the failure is really
	 "no backend".
	-CInformationElement gained mOriginalBlob, mbDirty and a static
	 sReencryptOnFormatChange hint set by MainWindow::save() right
	 before XMLPersister::save() walks the tree.
	-CTuxCardsConfiguration gained S_ENCRYPTION_FORMAT (string) and
	 B_REENCRYPT_ON_FORMAT_CHANGE (bool) — persisted under
	 [General] keys Encryption_Format and Reencrypt_On_Format_Change
	 in ~/.tuxcards.

3.1.1  2026-05-16  Packaging follow-up (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	-Build one native .deb per supported Debian/Ubuntu release
	 (ubuntu24.04, ubuntu26.04, debian12, debian13) via per-distro
	 GitHub Actions containers — Depends: now resolved against each
	 distro's Qt6/OpenSSL instead of a single Ubuntu 24.04 build.
	-Drop Fedora -debuginfo / -debugsource sub-packages from the
	 Release page (now disabled with all three rpm macros).
	-CMakeLists: install(TARGETS) declares BUNDLE DESTINATION so
	 macOS .app actually gets built; MACOSX_BUNDLE/WIN32_EXECUTABLE
	 forced TRUE on the tuxcards target.
	-Optional OpenSSL: TUXCARDS_WITH_OPENSSL CMake option. When OFF,
	 file encryption falls back to writing the legacy Blowfish format
	 (still readable by builds with OpenSSL).
	-Windows MSVC fixes: split the 16 600-byte Greetings.h literal
	 (C2026), const-corrected the static char * xpm arrays (C2440).
	-CI: Linux jobs run in distro containers with their own system
	 Qt6 (ubuntu:24.04, ubuntu:26.04, debian:12, debian:13). Portable
	 Linux tarball is bundled by hand via ldd+cp instead of the
	 flaky linuxdeployqt.

3.1.0  2026-05-16  Feature drop after 3.0.0 (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)

	Functional
	-Bookmarks bar pinned at the bottom of the window; entries
	 added via the tree's context menu, persisted across sessions in
	 the new "Bookmarks" config key.
	-RecentFileList rewritten on top of the cleaner CRecentFileList
	 design from TuxCards 2.2.1 (pre-created hidden QActions, paths in
	 QAction::data).
	-Toolbar visibility (View -> Toolbars) is now persisted between
	 sessions, with init-time writes guarded by mbStartupDone.
	-Search dialog: matched substring is highlighted in bold both in
	 the "Entry Name" and "Entry Content" columns via a new
	 SearchHighlightDelegate.

	Encryption
	-File encryption upgraded to AES-256-GCM with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256
	 (200000 iterations) via OpenSSL. Header magic "Fh_enc:AES256GCM-
	 PBKDF2", random 16-byte salt and 12-byte IV per file, 16-byte
	 GCM authentication tag.
	-Legacy "Fh_enc:BF10" (Blowfish + MD5(password)) is still
	 readable; the first save after decrypting an old file silently
	 upgrades the payload to the new format.

	Architecture & tooling
	-Build system switched to CMake. The legacy `tuxcards.pro`,
	 hand-written Makefile, qt-env-*.sh helpers and tests.pro are
	 removed. `qt_add_lupdate`/`qt_add_lrelease` integrate Qt
	 Linguist directly into the CMake build.
	-NULLPTR/NULL macros from src/global.h removed in favour of the
	 C++11 nullptr keyword (214 sites updated).
	-All Q3-era stamps ("//Added by qt3to4:") cleaned out.
	-Remaining German comments and identifiers ("Knoten",
	 "removeKnotenTool") translated/renamed; explanatory comments
	 added in three non-obvious places: CTreeElement::copyProperties
	 (why blockSignals), CInformationElement::~ (why qDeleteAll),
	 StringCrypter::encryptString (why we don't re-write legacy).
	-Packaging: debian/rules and rpm spec switched to CMake build.

	UX
	-Status bar shows "Saved Xs ago" / "Unsaved changes" /
	 "Saved just now", updated every second.
	-File menu: "Export current entry to Markdown..." and
	 "Import Markdown into current entry..." using
	 QTextDocument::toMarkdown()/setMarkdown() (Qt >=5.14).
	-Insert Image... (Ctrl+P) in Edit menu, back-ported from 2.2.1.
	-Bold/Italic/Underline/Color now also available as Edit menu
	 entries with Ctrl+B/I/U/M shortcuts; the toggle slots are
	 driven by the editor's current font state, so the same slots
	 work both from the toolbar and the menu.

	Tests & CI
	-QTest-based unit suites for StringCrypter (legacy + AES-GCM
	 round-trip, wrong-password, tampered-ciphertext, magic check),
	 ConfigParser and Path. Run via `ctest`.
	-GitHub Actions: build matrix Ubuntu 24.04 / Windows-latest /
	 macOS-latest on every push and PR, plus release workflow that
	 attaches .deb, .rpm, portable tar.xz, Windows .zip and
	 macOS .dmg to every `v*` tag.

	i18n
	-Translations for ten languages: en, ru, de, zh_CN, zh_TW, es,
	 fr, pt_BR, ja, ko. All 90 source strings translated where
	 meaningful (three are pure numbers/identifiers).
	-QTranslator loaded from the embedded ":/translations" resource
	 in main.cpp, locale-driven.

3.0.0  2026-05-16  Qt6 port (gzivdo + Claude Opus 4.7)
	-Full migration of the 2010.06.1 codebase from Qt 3 (Qt3Support) to Qt 6.
	-Back-ported CColorBar (left-side gradient sidebar) and the related
	 SideBar tab in the Options dialog from upstream TuxCards 2.2.1.
	-Back-ported PNG icons from 2.2.1 (file/edit/text/find/back/forward),
	 bundled through a Qt resource (src/icons/icons.qrc).
	-Search dialog re-laid out (650x380 default, "More >>>" toggle).
	-Editor: removed the Enter -> Ctrl+Enter remap, default QTextEdit
	 paragraph behavior; ASCII / RTF switch via setAcceptRichText.
	-Fixed: View -> Toolbars checkmarks now in sync with toolbar
	 visibility (toggled signal).
	-Fixed: Toggle file encryption correctly captures the entered
	 password (CPasswdDialog::verifyAndAccept).
	-Packaging: README.md, INSTALL.md, debian/ skeleton, rpm spec,
	 .desktop file.
	-About dialog mentions the Qt6 port and its initiator.

06-2010.1 amitch@rajgad.com

v2.1, amitch@rajgad.com
Major bug fixes
	-Ensure Auto save timer starts only when auto save is enabled. Without this, files were saved even from password prompt. Before this bug fix, if you are running two copies of Tuxcard with the same document open, one would over-write the changes by other.
Cleanups & Changes
	-Search: Added Search only titles. Allow Search dialog to be resizeable.
	-ESC works for Cancel when doing a Ctrl+N and prompt for non-dirty file. 
	-Remove expired entries feature
	-Multiple other minor bug fixes and changes.
	-Newer default toolbar icons
Encryption stuff
	-Remove encrypt active entry support
	-Removed auto encrypt support. 
	-Toggle button pressed on new after an encrypted file.
 
v2.0, amitch@rajgad.com
New:
-File encryption feature. This encryptes all the entries in the file and requires password on
	load. Accessible through toolbar, File menu and shortcut: CTRL+E
-Change text color for a single note or subtree of notes. New entries get subtree color of the parent, if set.
-Added a statusbar item for total number of notes\items.
-Added a dialog box under About menu to show current keyboard shortcuts.

Bug fixes
-Saveas did not work for unmodified files.
-The Base64 decoding had an off by one error which resulted in garabage characters at end of some newly 
decrypted entries. (Not mine)
-Better search results, Show string starting with the matched text and ensure it does not go over a certain 
	limit (80 chars). This results in better visiblity on the found items and no wrap-around resulting in 
	unreadable text.
-Fixed bug of losing unsaved text when dragging and dropping an item. 
-Allow selecting notes with same names(title.)
-Fixed bug of incorrect end calculation in CBlowFish::Encode when using same buffer for 
		encrypted and decrypted data
-Crash on encrypted data size == 0.  (Happens only for dev code)
-Incorrect flagging newly opened file as dirty.

Other minor changes
-When a new note is created or dropped drop, focus now moves to new item.
-Added a menu item for F2(Rename in place edit of tree item.)
-Disabled autoformatting in editor to convert text like - into bullet items.
-Search dialog: Added accelator keys and set main button as default. This also adds support for Enter 
  and ESC key. SearchDialog::SearchDialog()
-Removed unpolite references such as "sorry" from confirm delete dialogbox, "Freaks" from About box.
  Other minor changes in toolbar text, etc.
-Modified qmake file, tuxcards.pro to "make install" work correctly, installs docs and icons. Update tuxcards.pro
 to change DESTDIR.

 
v1.2, 
A lot of minor changes provide an easier overall usage of TuxCards. For details look at "Improvments in Detail"; here are some key features:
 -Entry History. It does work like a history within a web browser; the last visited entries are remembered.
 -Encryption using MD5 and BlowFish. The encrypted data is stored using Base64 encoding.
 -Selection of information format (rtf, txt) for newly created entries.
 -Inplace renaming of entries within the tree.
 -Customized line break mode. Keys for creating a new line or new paragraph within the editor may be selected.
 -Much better paste algorithm for pasting text within the editor.
 -Improved HTML export.
 -Several new keyboard shortcuts.
 -Nice Look & Feel (supporting keramic style and customizable icons)
 -An alternative set of icons may already be downloaded from www.tuxcards.de.
 -Increased overall stability.
 